[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
To finish installing the SamDrucker website:

1. Let the reporting role read the package tables, and create a login
   for the website in that role. Both are in:

     %%DATADIR%%/updates-website.sql

   Run it as the owner of the SamDrucker tables. Allow the new login
   from this host in pg_hba.conf.

2. Put that login's details in:

     %%ETCDIR%%/samdruckerweb.conf

   That file must be readable by www and no one else.

3. Point your web server at %%WWWDIR%%/www
   and nowhere above it. There is a sample nginx configuration in:

     %%DATADIR%%/nginx-config.conf

   It requires a password. Create the password file before reloading
   nginx, or every request gets a 500 error:

     sudo install -m 640 -o root -g www /dev/null \
         %%PREFIX%%/etc/nginx/samdruckerweb.htpasswd
     printf 'dan:%s\n' "$(openssl passwd -6)" | \
         sudo tee -a %%PREFIX%%/etc/nginx/samdruckerweb.htpasswd > /dev/null

   It also gives the website access and error logs of its own, named
   after its hostname. They are rotated by:

     %%PREFIX%%/etc/newsyslog.conf.d/samdruckerweb.conf

   which matches /var/log/nginx/samdruckerweb*.log; edit it if your
   hostname does not start with samdruckerweb.

The website lists the exact package versions on every host, which tells
anyone who can read it what each host is vulnerable to. Serve it on an
internal network only, behind the password.

More detail: %%DATADIR%%/README.md
EOM
}
]
